      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, I think this is actively harmful on CI machines.\n\nThe way that \"build_error.log\" operates, it parses stdout for any output that \"looks like an error\", and then trunctates the log to be a certain number of lines. In practice, a lot of the lines that would display with `-x` \"look like an error\", so using `-x` ends up making build_error.log unusuable.\n\nI\u0027ve started moving our other scripts to omit `-x` for this purpose. This is a step in the wrong direction there.\n\nIn the future, you can run `bash -x tests/run_integration_tests.sh` to add this option to a one-off local run for debugging purposes.",
      "revId": "7c04e368de5ed295f3c4cd5138d7976ce8cb8109",
